[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MOS memory execution and nonlinear trapezoidal history

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Implementation and verification trace: MOS1 junction lowering and startup are in
dotnet/Simulator.Frontend/Mos1Preparation.cs, TransientSelection.cs and
RequestedAnalysis.cs, verified by MosMemoryPreparationTests.cs and the original
memory replay. Endpoint equations/history and audits are in src/newton.rs,
src/configured.rs, src/api.rs and src/audit_configured.rs; independent equations,
negative histories, retry rollback and observer accounting are exercised by
tests/nonlinear_trapezoidal.rs. Periodic corners are in src/waveform.rs and
src/sources.rs. Current-error policies are in src/adaptive.rs with unit and
integration properties. Homogeneous projection is in src/backend.rs, its unit
tests and tests/lu_zero_constraints.rs. Explicit provider qualification is in
RequestedCorpus.cs and RequestedQualificationTests.cs. Bounded evidence and
coverage limits are in evidence/mos-memory-execution.json and
docs/mos-memory-results.md. All requirements remain Draft: finite evidence does
not establish general numerical bounds or stock-default memory-deck parity.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOS1-JUNCTION-GMIN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit MOS1 junction conductance
STATEMENT: >>>
The default ngspice-compatible MOS1 package shall retain 1e-12 S across each
nondegenerate intrinsic body junction in DC, AC and transient. Lowering shall
make these branches explicit to independent physical audits and drain sensors.
This junction compatibility floor shall remain distinct from temporary global
Gmin continuation, whose final physical solve removes its extra nodal shunts.
Explicit nondefault Gmin cards remain unsupported until separately qualified.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-NONLINEAR-TRAP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Endpoint nonlinear trapezoidal equations
STATEMENT: >>>
Nonlinear trapezoidal integration shall balance endpoint conduction and the
signed charge difference, using the complete previous excitation and committed
state. Each Newton trial shall preserve history. Junction total-current
reporting shall use the same accepted discrete method. An independent audit
shall reconstruct endpoint KCL and nonlinear junction charge without production
residuals or Jacobians, and explicitly identify unavailable energy/model audits.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-CORNER-RESTART-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: First-order restart at source corners
STATEMENT: >>>
A nonlinear trapezoidal run shall use a first-order interval at startup and
immediately after source breakpoints to avoid propagating alternating endpoint
currents from an abrupt slope change. Actual accepted restart endpoints shall
be retained for independent audits and current reconstruction. Rejected trials
shall not publish state, restart evidence or source history.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-CURRENT-ACCURACY-FLOOR-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Report a stricter physical-consistency convergence floor
STATEMENT: >>>
A requested ABSTOL shall bound permitted current convergence error without
weakening the runtime's existing physical-consistency accuracy floor. A stricter
authored current bound shall remain effective. The input shall retain its
original value and the integration report shall disclose the actual step bound.
Fixed and removed continuation conductances shall remain distinct. Neither
independent audit tolerances nor reference-comparison tolerances may be widened
to make a run pass.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-ACCEPTED-MIDPOINTS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Retain accepted adaptive history for physical evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
An adaptive configured run shall retain its actual accepted first-half-step
state for each output interval, within the aggregate stored-state budget.
Independent API audits shall evaluate both accepted half steps; derived
junction currents shall reconstruct the endpoint using that same retained
history and actual BE/trapezoidal restart methods. Rejected trials shall never
enter output or audit history. Reporting shall disclose retained midpoint count;
standalone endpoint-only audit calls shall continue to identify missing history.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-DAE-ERROR-STATES-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: State and derivative-current error budgets
STATEMENT: >>>
The adaptive controller shall distinguish the first-order derivative startup
from subsequent trapezoidal work. A restart shall establish current accuracy
using one quarter of the ordinary current-error budget, leaving headroom for
the derivative recurrence. Subsequent error checks shall retain every voltage
and branch current, including algebraic source/sensor observers and inductor
flux currents. Shape and finite-value checks shall include every unknown.
Newton, independent current/KCL and reference bounds shall remain unchanged.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-ADAPTIVE-RETRY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded recovery from numerical trial failures
STATEMENT: >>>
Only a numerical or singular trial failure inside an explicit adaptive budget
may reject and reduce the attempted interval. Malformed, unsupported, cancelled
and other terminal failures shall propagate. Minimum step and attempt ceilings
shall remain enforced; state, midpoint history, source RHS, restart evidence
and observer output shall publish only after acceptance. Provider-call counts
shall include failed trials and initialization without double counting.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-LU-HOMOGENEOUS-CONSTRAINTS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact homogeneous constraint projection with unchanged acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
Dense LU refinement shall preserve exact zero-RHS singleton and equal-coefficient
opposite-sign two-term constraints, including transitive zero-voltage sensing
chains. Candidate projection shall remain finite and bounded, and shall never
change matrix coefficients, RHS values or the full-system 1e-10 componentwise
backward-error acceptance bound. Nonzero RHS and unequal coefficients shall not
be admitted as homogeneous equalities. A corrected candidate shall still pass
verification against the complete original system.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRANSIENT-CURRENT-RELATIVE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit current-observer relative budget
STATEMENT: >>>
Adaptive current relative accuracy may be specified separately from voltage
relative accuracy. An absent current-relative value shall retain the historical
shared relative value. A specified value shall be finite, positive and below
one. Every branch current shall remain controlled; a separate budget shall not
remove current checks or change independent audit/reference tolerances. The
normal requested MOS1 profile shall disclose its voltage and current budgets
on the typed request rather than infer a weaker comparison after execution.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-QUALIFICATION-EXPLICIT-CPU-PROVIDER-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit CPU provider qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
The requested-corpus coordinator shall accept an explicit supported CPU backend,
retain the existing LU default, place the selected backend on every ordinary
request and record it in the report. An unsupported provider shall be rejected
before output creation. A failed provider shall not silently select another;
provider-specific failures and available comparisons shall remain distinct.
<<<
